      "writtenOn": "2023-09-08T18:06:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s two ways to define JNI functions:\n\n1. A full name that matches the class you want to register against. i.e. `pub extern \"system\" fn com_android_bluetooth_btservice_AdapterNativeInterface_testFoo`\n2. Call `register_native_methods` with the fn you want to use.\n\nI\u0027m opting to do the latter because I want to be able to change between two implementations at runtime using an Android flag.",
      "parentUuid": "9101cc9d_75d21593",
